schema: "0.4"
id: trd-authoring-03-creation-palette
type: image
quality: high

# therobotdrafts authoring UX — creation palette (kind picker) detail mockup.
# Consumes: design-conventions §1.1 silhouettes + §2.1 Okabe-Ito palette + §2.4
# redundancy/colorblind rules, Lena's §C kind glyph set (e94fe1b8), Yuki's
# add-node flow (abf97287): containment-filtered, name-on-create.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity DETAIL mockup of a
    "creation palette" — the kind picker for adding an element to a 3D bubble UML
    IDE. Premium, calm, technical. The palette's job: let the user pick an element
    KIND, where each row's swatch is the EXACT hue + silhouette the new 3D bubble
    will have, so picking is previewing. Colorblind-safe: every kind is separated
    by SHAPE as well as hue (meaning survives if color is removed).
  text: |
    A 4:3 close-up mockup: a creation palette flyout open over a softly-blurred
    dark 3D bubble-view background, mid add-node interaction.

    BACKGROUND (blurred, secondary):
    - Dark graphite 3D space; a translucent frosted slate Package bubble (#6E7B8B)
      is the TARGET PARENT, shown with the valid-target affordance: a white rim +
      a faint ✓ ghost + a subtle snap-pulse ring (reserved UI channel — NOT a kind
      color). A faint dashed ghost of a new bubble previews where it will pack
      inside the parent.

    THE CREATION PALETTE (sharp foreground, dark translucent graphite panel,
    rounded, soft drop shadow):
    - Title row: small muted label "Add element" + a tiny notation tag "UML".
    - A vertical list of kind rows, each = [colored kind glyph] [name] [hint],
      using the exact §2.1 hue AND a distinct monochrome-readable silhouette:
        ○ Package    slate #6E7B8B   (dashed circle, nested dots — "container")
        ● Class      blue  #0072B2   (solid filled circle)         ← ROW HIGHLIGHTED (default), white→cyan selection rim
        ◐ Interface  sky   #56B4E9   (circle with open equatorial band)
        ⬢ Enum       orange #E69F00  (hexagon / faceted)
        ◑ Struct     teal  #009E73   (circle with flat top chord)
        ·  Function  green #2CA02C   (small solid dot)
        ·  Field     yellow-green #BCBD22 (small flattened ellipse)  ← ROW DIMMED + struck, with a small "illegal in Package" reason chip
    - A small footer toggle "[ abstract ]" (a wireframe-outline modifier) shown
      unchecked.
    - The highlighted Class row shows a tiny inline NAME field with a blinking
      caret and a ghost preview "Class1" — name-on-create: the element is placed
      and immediately namable.

    DESIGN NOTES TO HONOR:
    - Each swatch is literally a small render of that kind's bubble (hue+silhouette),
      so the palette previews the result.
    - The illegal kind (Field, not allowed directly in a Package) is DIMMED with a
      reason, never hidden — it teaches the containment rule.
    - Panel chrome is achromatic graphite/white; the ONLY colors are the kind
      swatches and the white→cyan selection rim.
    - Clean humanist sans-serif, crisp at small size; generous row spacing; ≥32px
      row targets.

    MOOD: precise, calm, premium developer tool. Not a game menu, not playful.
  provider_options:
    aspect_ratio: "4:3"
    style: "natural"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1600
    height: 1200
    aspect_ratio: "4:3"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    kind_swatches: {weight: 3, description: "Seven UML-core kind rows, each with the exact Okabe-Ito hue AND a distinct silhouette glyph (frosted package, solid class, banded interface, hexagon enum, polar-cap struct, dot function, flat field) — colorblind-separable by shape"}
    states_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Class row highlighted with white→cyan rim + inline name caret (name-on-create); Field row dimmed/struck with an 'illegal in parent' reason; target parent shows white-rim + ✓ valid affordance"}
    reserved_channel: {weight: 2, description: "Panel chrome achromatic; only kind swatches + white→cyan selection carry color; no UI tinted as a kind hue"}
    premium_detail: {weight: 2, description: "Crisp legible rows, premium calm dev-tool styling, generous spacing"}
  reject_if:
    - "kinds distinguished by color only (no distinct silhouettes)"
    - "illegal kind hidden instead of dimmed-with-reason"
    - "palette chrome tinted with kind colors or rainbow"
    - "game/playful menu aesthetic"

tags: [trd, authoring-ux, creation-palette, kind-picker, bubble-view, uml, mockup]
